<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 25,644,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 25,644,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 04/23/97    04/16/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 25,644,000  26,203,000    25,863,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  97,814	63,762	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   04/23/97    04/16/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,999,000   4,358,000     4,202,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,808,000   4,619,000     4,571,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,158,000   4,184,000     4,713,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,394,000   2,220,000     2,645,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,526,000   3,767,000     3,232,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,919,000   4,997,000     4,897,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,840,000   2,058,000     1,603,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	25,644,000  26,203,000    25,863,000</p>
